tract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [tester] tester (codex) (run=RUN-260730-3716a5, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [tester] tester (codex) (run=RUN-260730-3716a5)\nTESTER DIAGNOSIS 2026-07-30 cycle 5: Native ssh win probe reproduced the worker failure before Go. The inherited launch pipe was present at handle 528 with the exact 88-byte csk-go-launch-v1 record, but the manager PID was 13192 while the executing worker PID 2136 reported parent PID 2780. Windows venv Scripts/python.exe is a redirector process, so _parse_worker_launch_record rejects direct-child ownership; cli.main then falls through to argparse (exit 2, invalid hidden choice), and the manager later receives BrokenPipeError at _write_message. Minimal defensible fix is the candidate already appearing in the producer worktree: on Windows launch the identity-bound runtime.base_executable.path, keep the installed csk.exe as the fixed script/mode, and accept/prove that bound base process image. Required regression: synthetic Windows venv identity asserts worker_argv selects base_executable, plus native Windows capability/fixture proof that hidden dispatch remains alive and accepted builds pass. Diagnostic scripts/logs will be attached in the tester outcome; no product source edited.\nTESTER FOLLOW-UP 2026-07-30: Producer candidate closes the venv redirector ancestry defect, but native rerun still has 3 accepted-case failures: worker now returns build_execution_worker_identity_invalid installed manager launcher is unavailable. Native console-archive overlay proves distlib rewrites sys.argv[0] from ...\Scripts\csk.exe to the nonexistent extensionless ...\Scripts\csk before csk.cli.main, while sys.orig_argv remains exactly [base python.exe, -S, -s, -B, -P, installed csk.exe, __csk-go-worker-v1]. Therefore run_worker defaults worker_executable to a nonexistent path. Minimal closed fix: after consuming the authenticated launch capability, derive/pass worker_executable from the one validated fixed sys.orig_argv launcher slot (or an equally closed fixed-argv helper), then let expected manager identity matching reject any discrepancy; do not use extensionless sys.argv[0]. Required unit negative/positive: fixed orig argv selects csk.exe; malformed, extra, reordered, programmatic, or non-capability argv never dispatches. Required native rerun: all accepted Windows fixture cases. Diagnostic command exit 0; no product source edited.\nTESTER CYCLE-5 CLOSURE 2026-07-30: After the redirector and distlib launcher fixes, native candidate4 exposed an unavoidable Windows Python-home sys.path entry. Allowing it unbound would admit root-level code before proof, so the defensible fix binds the complete bounded python_home import tree while excluding site-package trees disabled by -S/-s. Tester regression first exited 1 with 2 failures: stale startup-root deserialization and omitted existing python314.zip; after exact _manager_runtime_roots validation and fixed-slot archive binding it exited 0 with 2 passed. Unchanged candidate6 Windows fixture exited 0: 5 passed/5 host skips, all 3 accepted variants plus hidden-literal/runtime-image negatives. Independent tester plain accepted fixture exited 0: 1 passed/no skips in 63.33s. Local focused pytest 118 passed/1 skip, strict mypy 65 files, compileall, and tabnanny all exited 0. Whole-module unit branch coverage measured 54%, so the 80% whole-file checklist item remains unchecked. Evidence and exact commands are in TASK-260720-2g21eg_tester-windows-worker-diagnosis.md and attached JUnit outcomes.\nTESTER EXACT-CANDIDATE ADDENDUM 2026-07-30: Candidate 8 wheel SHA-256 8cc70ef4ef574088c0c017905b6a5609820a6f2bdc3e984b6b1669674ba9af4f contains go_v1.py SHA-256 abdf349c3ff2ebad7f17c25480655e65134378b1a402c7de9e010de3a684fcd4, byte-equal to handoff source. Native macOS fixture exit 0: 10 passed/no skips, JUnit 63.985s. Native Windows exact-wheel fixture exit 0: 5 passed/5 host skips, JUnit 287.548s. Independent tester Windows accepted case on the same installed candidate exit 0: 1 passed/no skips in 62.09s. Exact final local exits: focused pytest 0 (119 passed/1 skip), strict mypy 0 (65 files), compileall 0, tabnanny 0, git diff --check 0, explicit untracked-file whitespace/conflict scan 0. Refreshed whole-module branch coverage remains 54% (3093 statements, 1313 missed; 1050 branches, 214 partial), so item 15 remains honestly unchecked.\nTESTER AFFECTED-COVERAGE CLOSURE 2026-07-30: Operator clarified item 15 as cycle-5 affected/change scope, not the whole new driver. Initial reviewed-cycle4-to-cycle5 measurement exited 0 but was below target: 197/291 changed lines (67.70%), 61/106 branches (57.55%), 258/397 combined (64.99%); item remained unchecked. After narrow regression additions only, final focused pytest exited 0 with 139 passed/1 skip and the same standalone measurement exited 0 at 271/291 changed lines (93.13%), 94/106 branches (88.68%), 365/397 combined (91.94%). Item 15 is now checked. Whole-module branch-aware coverage is separately reported as 57%, with no 80% whole-module claim.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260730-5534f8, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (run=RUN-260730-5534f8)\nREVIEW VERDICT CYCLE 5 2026-07-30: accepted. Independent reviewer (claude, RUN-260730-5534f8) rebuilt the wheel from the worktree (installed go_v1.py byte-identical to source and to tester candidate-8: abdf349c...), and ran all gates standalone on macOS arm64 / Go 1.25.5: focused unit pytest with the accepted rc.5 conformance root 140 passed/0 skipped exit 0; strict configured mypy 65 files exit 0; native wheel-installed real-Go fixture 10 passed in 71.74s exit 0 covering all accepted variants, runtime-image/stdlib/package/startup-hook/worker-executable mutation negatives, teardown failure, and poisoned-PATH hidden-literal parser rejection with the never-run marker absent; git diff --check / tabnanny / whitespace clean. Cycle-2 and cycle-4 blocking findings verified closed in code (framework runtime-image binding, per-operation five-probe measurement, Windows pyvenv.cfg base runtime + base-executable launch + distlib argv0 recovery + bounded python_home tree). AC verified against the vectors: exact source-aware argv, 13 states, one-list/one-permit/one-build, fixed environment, 18 mandatory controls, closed capability evidence with all 8 rules, failure boundary, 6 deferred guards, 14+8+11 named cases, one non-DepOnly main package, bounded never-run output, non-macOS/Windows fail-closed. Non-blocking caveats: native Windows evidence is tester candidate-8 (same go_v1.py bytes), CI re-verification remains the standing follow-up; whole-module coverage 57% with affected-scope 91.94% per operator clarification; evidence-record exposure surfaces are downstream TASK-260720-2x6mjn scope. Verdict evidence: TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-5.md plus reviewer-cycle5 JUnit XMLs. Route done.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260730-5534f8, pid=89922, exit=0)\nPOST-ACCEPTANCE CI REWORK 2026-07-30: GitHub PR #12 strict mypy on ubuntu failed with 13 attr-defined errors for Darwin-only select.kqueue/KQ_NOTE_*, os.O_EVTONLY, select.kevent/KQ_FILTER_VNODE/KQ_EV_* symbols at go_v1.py:3731-3758. Local macOS mypy had passed because platform stubs expose them. Route narrow cross-platform typing correction to developer, rerun Linux-equivalent mypy plus focused tests, then independent review and update the signed PR commit.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composit