EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_csk-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-2g21eg_go-v1-compile-driver/progress.md:120:TESTER DIAGNOSIS 2026-07-30 cycle 5: Native ssh win probe reproduced the worker failure before Go. The inherited launch pipe was present at handle 528 with the exact 88-byte csk-go-launch-v1 record, but the manager PID was 13192 while the executing worker PID 2136 reported parent PID 2780. Windows venv Scripts/python.exe is a redirector process, so _parse_worker_launch_record rejects direct-child ownership; cli.main then falls through to argparse (exit 2, invalid hidden choice), and the manager later receives BrokenPipeError at _write_message. Minimal defensible fix is the candidate already appearing in the producer worktree: on Windows launch the identity-bound runtime.base_executable.path, keep the installed csk.exe as the fixed script/mode, and accept/prove that bound base process image. Required regression: synthetic Windows venv identity asserts worker_argv selects base_executable, plus native Windows capability/fixture proof that hidden dispatch remains alive and accepted builds pass. Diagnostic scripts/logs will be attached in the tester outcome; no product source edited.
EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_csk-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-2g21eg_go-v1-compile-driver/progress.md-121-TESTER FOLLOW-UP 2026-07-30: Producer candidate closes the venv redirector ancestry defect, but native rerun still has 3 accepted-case failures: worker now returns build_execution_worker_identity_invalid installed manager launcher is unavailable. Native console-archive overlay proves distlib rewrites sys.argv[0] from ...\Scripts\csk.exe to the nonexistent extensionless ...\Scripts\csk before csk.cli.main, while sys.orig_argv remains exactly [base python.exe, -S, -s, -B, -P, installed csk.exe, __csk-go-worker-v1]. Therefore run_worker defaults worker_executable to a nonexistent path. Minimal closed fix: after consuming the authenticated launch capability, derive/pass worker_executable from the one validated fixed sys.orig_argv launcher slot (or an equally closed fixed-argv helper), then let expected manager identity matching reject any discrepancy; do not use extensionless sys.argv[0]. Required unit negative/positive: fixed orig argv selects csk.exe; malformed, extra, reordered, programmatic, or non-capability argv never dispatches. Required native rerun: all accepted Windows fixture cases. Diagnostic command exit 0; no product source edited.
