+### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 cycle-6 CI portability closure
+- CI FINDING: PR 12 exposed test-only host assumptions after the accepted cycle-5 product candidate: Ubuntu correctly rejected synthetic manager identities through the unsupported production resolver, Windows synthetic fixtures described a POSIX interpreter layout, and several platform-specific assertions ran on the wrong host. Linux strict mypy also saw Darwin-only kqueue symbols through Linux stubs.
+- REWORK: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` keeps the product support boundary closed over exactly macOS and Windows. A test-only unsupported-host runtime seam preserves broad protocol coverage while a separate captured production-resolver negative proves Linux still fails with `build_execution_control_unavailable`. Windows fixtures now model base CPython, its one runtime DLL, `Lib`, and the installed manager tree; POSIX-only shebang/process-group assertions and chmod/path presentation are host-aware. Darwin kqueue access uses runtime-preserving casts solely at the type-checking boundary.
+- NATIVE WINDOWS: a push-free exact-byte snapshot on `ssh win` matched the local two-file overlay and pinned rc.5 archive hashes. Focused pytest exited 0 with 131 passed / 10 skips, and full pytest exited 0 with 1064 passed / 116 skips. The task-owned remote root and staging inputs were removed and absence verified.
+- HOST GATES: final macOS focused pytest exited 0 with 141 passed; full pytest exited 0 with 1159 passed / 21 skips; the wheel-installed native Go 1.25.5 fixture exited 0 with 10 passed. Configured and Linux-target strict mypy passed 65 files; unsupported-Linux focused selection passed 129 / skipped 12; build, Twine, compileall, tabnanny, and diff hygiene exited 0.
